     "rule": "The quietest text.",
     "pick": "neutral.500: the quietest text that still reads, 7.0:1 on surface.default, above the 7:1 floor.",
     "darkPick": "neutral.600: We use the quietest readable gray for hints and captions in dark in order to keep muted text a step below secondary text (neutral.700). The step does this by reading 7.67:1 on surface.default and 6.09:1 on surface.raised, the lightest surface it meets. Raised layers fall under 7:1 by the owner's recorded exception for muted text, the one light mode takes too, as the next gray up is secondary's own step. So people read a hint in a menu as well as on the page, because text keeps the AAA floor (accessibility.definition) and the neutral ramp has no step between muted and secondary (color.definition).",
